<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Writing Studio: third-party notices</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; max-width: 46em; margin: 2em auto; padding: 0 1em; color: #24211c; background: #fbf8f1; line-height: 1.5; }
h1, h2, h3 { font-weight: 600; }
pre { white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 0.85em; background: #f1ebdd; padding: 1em; }
ul.crates { columns: 2; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { background: #1d1c1a; color: #e6e0d4; } pre { background: #2a2824; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Writing Studio: third-party notices</h1>
<p>Writing Studio is free and open source under the MIT or Apache-2.0 license, at your choice. Its source is at https://github.com/jjdias/writing-studio.</p>
<p>It is built from the open-source libraries below, each under the license shown with it. Two of them, <strong>spellbook</strong> (https://github.com/helix-editor/spellbook) and <strong>option-ext</strong> (https://github.com/soc/option-ext), are under the Mozilla Public License 2.0. Writing Studio uses them unchanged, and their source is at those addresses.</p>
<p>The English (US) spelling dictionary comes from the Hunspell and SCOWL word lists, under its own license, in <code>dictionary-LICENSE.txt</code> beside this file. Writing Studio's own licenses are in <code>LICENSE-MIT</code> and <code>LICENSE-APACHE</code>.</p>

<h2>Licenses</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
<li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

{{#each licenses}}
<h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul class="crates">
{{#each used_by}}
<li>{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
